{"id": "Dfhcc1XktNW", "title": "Video by vedastovikings", "description": "For one year, Arjuna lived as a woman in a king's palace. If anyone recognised him, twelve more years of exile.\nएक साल तक... अर्जुन एक राजमहल में स्त्री बनकर रहे। अगर कोई पहचान लेता... तो बारह साल का वनवास फिर से।\n\nThe stake of the last game of dice: twelve years in the forest, the thirteenth hidden among people, or twelve years more. So the Pandavas hid as servants in King Virata's palace: Yudhishthira a dice-playing Brahmin, Bhima the cook, Nakula and Sahadeva with the horses and cattle, Draupadi the queen's maid, and Arjuna, by Urvashi's curse, a dance teacher, neither man nor woman. Then Kichaka laid hands on Draupadi, and Bhima killed him in the night. In Hastinapura the news reached Duryodhana, and Karna said the Pandavas were dead, not knowing they were his own brothers. They came to raid Virata's cattle, not knowing who was waiting. (Mahabharata, Sabha 2.76; Vana 3.46; Virata Parva 4.1-30; Udyoga 5.140)\n\nThe Brother Who Never Knew, Part 7. Part 8, The Dance Teacher: the whole Kuru army against one frightened prince, and his dance teacher.\n\nDid you know Arjuna spent a year as a dancer? Tell me below 👇\n\n#mahabharat #mahabharata #arjuna #karna #महाभारत", "channel": "vedastovikings", "uploader_id": "60997589521", "uploader": "Vedas to Vikings | Mythology films", "timestamp": 1794231143, "like_count": 1613, "comment_count": 4, "http_headers": {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/147.0.0.0 Safari/537.36", "Accept": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml,application/xml;q=0.9,*/*;q=0.8", "Accept-Language": "en-us,en;q=0.5", "Sec-Fetch-Mode": "navigate", "Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-17960463171037522a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 66.886, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr2-3.fna.fbcd